1. NIST test vectors (CAVP / ACVP)
----------------------------------

The golden-model data directories contain test-vector files obtained from the
National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) Automated Cryptographic
Validation Protocol (ACVP) / Cryptographic Algorithm Validation Program (CAVP):

  - ecdsa-keygen            (ECDSA keyGen)
  - kas-ecc-cdh-component   (KAS-ECC CDH-Component)
  - kas-ecc-p192            (KAS-ECC; includes files derived from the NIST data)

Source: National Institute of Standards and Technology. The vectors are used
here only to validate the golden model and the RTL. The source is
acknowledged explicitly: NIST is the source of these vectors.

Modifications: some files in these directories were reformatted, filtered or
converted by scripts of this project (for example parse_nist.py and the
derived nist_p256_vectors.json). Such files are modified works. They were
created in 2026 and differ from the NIST originals in format and selection of
entries, not in the cryptographic values.

